  "caveat": "These are separate reconstructions of separate animals at separate stages, so a smaller edge count at L1 means 'this many were reconstructed', not 'the animal had this many'.  Single L1 files carry ~570-800 distinct edges against ~1,100 for a single L2 file and ~1,550 for an adult, so the L1 numbers are a floor.  The conclusion this artifact is offered for -- the four circuits are already wired at the earliest stage and gain synapse count afterwards -- is the one that survives that confound; the 271 edge pairs seen in L1 and absent from adults (`stage_diffs.l1_only_keys`) are NOT reported as transient synapses, because that difference is confounded with reconstruction depth.",
